ulah and San Isabel.\n\nThis includes the following high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.","ends":"2026-09-29T19:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ed2cf324071318d953e2a918a3c1b27003277e15.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ed2cf324071318d953e2a918a3c1b27003277e15.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 29 at 11:59AM MDT until October 1 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The Southeast Mountains, the Wet Mountain Valley, eastern\nFremont county and the southeast plains.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rainfall associated with a remnant tropical\nstorm system will spread across southern Colorado through\nThursday.\n\n- The Southeast Mountains, including the Aspen Acres burn area, the\nWet Mountain Valley, eastern Fremont county, and the southeast\nplains.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-01T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains Between 8500 And 11000 Ft; Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains above 11000 Ft; Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Between 7500 and 11000 Ft; Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Above 11000 Ft; Western/Central Fremont County Below 8500 Ft; Wet Mountain Valley Below 8500 Ft; Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Canon City Vicinity/Eastern Fremont County; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft; Crowley